title: The bill, and what dominated it
subtitle: Week 22 - read from Cost Explorer by usage type on 2026-10-09, not from a rate card
width: 1080
---
$ aws ce get-cost-and-usage --granularity DAILY \
      --filter '{"Dimensions":{"Key":"SERVICE","Values":["Amazon EC2 Container Registry (ECR)"]}}' \
      --group-by Type=DIMENSION,Key=USAGE_TYPE

  2026-10-06   USE1-AsyncActions-ImageSigning   $0.2400   qty 12
  2026-10-06   TimedStorage-ByteHrs             $0.0002
  2026-10-07   TimedStorage-ByteHrs             $0.0003
  2026-10-08   TimedStorage-ByteHrs             $0.0003
  2026-10-09   TimedStorage-ByteHrs             $0.0001   (destroyed 14:21)

  TOTAL                                         $0.2409

  signing   $0.2400   ###############################################  99.7%
  storage   $0.0009   #                                                 0.3%

$ ... --group-by Type=DIMENSION,Key=SERVICE  | grep -E 'Inspector|CodeBuild'

  Amazon Inspector   0      [ok] 15-day free trial, started 2026-10-05
  CodeBuild          0      [ok] free tier

--- the part that is not on any pricing page -----------------------------

ECR bills managed signing as USE1-AsyncActions-ImageSigning at $0.02 per
signature. Twelve signatures, because four builds each signed three images:
every rebuild re-signs.

AWS Signer's pricing page says "no additional charge" with ECR. That is true
of Signer. The charge is ECR's, and ECR's pricing page carries a "Managed
Signing" heading with no figure under it.

I wrote "signing is free" in the draft of this post. The bill is the only
place the number appeared.
